    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d684">

                <pb facs="0779" n="659" xml:id="pg659"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/396: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reber</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-16T16:00:00-00:44">January 16, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>9. I am told by the British Chargé that he has been instructed to cooperate with
                    me in strong representations to the Government here. In view of his telegram
                    stating that instructions have already been sent me regarding procedure to be
                    adopted, should I regard the second paragraph of the Department’s No. 6, January
                    12, 2 [<hi rendition="#italic">1</hi>] p.m., as containing these instructions,
                    which are to be supplemented by the Department’s further expression of views in
                    regard to the ineffectiveness of the Liberian reform program?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reber</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
